      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: `targets.insert` will always return `true` because `target_ref` is a completely new allocation via `FakeTargetRef::new(target)`. \n\n`FakeTargetRef`\u0027s `Hash` and `Eq` implementation is based on pointer equality, not value equality of its inner `FakeTarget`. As a result, the `assert!` will never trigger, allowing multiple targets with the same label and toolchain to be inserted into the set, which contradicts the intention and the panic message.\n\nIf the goal was to deduplicate by label/toolchain, keeping a `HashMap\u003c(Label, Label), FakeTargetRef\u003e` would be much safer.",
