      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: Adding `unsafe impl Send` and `unsafe impl Sync` to a type that relies on `Rc` and `RefCell` is very risky. \n\nIf this type is ever sent across threads (for instance, by parallel test runners), it will lead to race conditions (e.g., data races on the `Rc` reference count) and Undefined Behavior. \n\nIf the compiler does not demand `Send` / `Sync` because `FakeTargetRef` never crosses threads, these implementations are redundant and misleading. If the compiler does demand them, then `Arc` and `Mutex` are required and replacing them with `Rc`/`RefCell` is a bug.",
